---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Laravel Valet (macOS)"
  path="/dev/laravel-valet"
  section="dev"
  description="Run KoAkademy locally with Valet's classic minimal PHP environment on macOS."
>
  <p>
    Valet is the lightweight classic: PHP and Nginx on macOS with automatic
    <code>.test</code> domains and no database management. Herd is the newer, actively
    developed alternative that bundles PHP, Node, and database services — most macOS
    users should prefer
    <a href="/dev/laravel-herd">Herd</a>. This guide covers Valet for those who
    already use it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Install</h2>
  <pre><code>brew install php
composer global require laravel/valet
valet install</code></pre>
  <p>
    Valet requires PHP 8.3 or newer; KoAkademy targets PHP 8.5, which
    <code>brew install php</code> provides. Make sure the Composer
    <code>vendor/bin</code> directory is on your <code>PATH</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Park and clone</h2>
  <pre><code>mkdir -p ~/Sites
valet park ~/Sites
cd ~/Sites
git clone https://github.com/yukazakiri/koakademy.git
cd koakademy
composer install
npm ci
cp .env.example .env
php artisan key:generate</code></pre>
  <p>
    Every folder inside a parked directory becomes a site, so KoAkademy is
    served at <code>http://koakademy.test</code>. Projects outside a parked
    directory can be registered with <code>valet link</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Database</h2>
  <p>Valet does not manage databases. Two options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>SQLite (simplest):</strong>
      <pre><code>touch database/database.sqlite</code></pre>
      In <code>.env</code>, set <code>DB_CONNECTION=sqlite</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>PostgreSQL via Homebrew:</strong>
      <pre><code>brew install postgresql@16
brew services start postgresql@16
createdb koakademy</code></pre>
      In <code>.env</code>, set <code>DB_CONNECTION=pgsql</code>,
      <code>DB_HOST=127.0.0.1</code>, <code>DB_PORT=5432</code>,
      <code>DB_DATABASE=koakademy</code>, <code>DB_USERNAME</code> to your macOS username,
      and an empty password for the default local trust setup.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For queues, cache, or sessions, install Redis the same way (<code
      >brew install redis</code
    > and
    <code>brew services start redis</code>) and point
    <code>REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Migrate, secure, and serve</h2>
  <pre><code>php artisan migrate
valet secure</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>valet secure</code> serves the site over HTTPS with a trusted local certificate
    (<code>https://koakademy.test</code>). Run
    <code>npm run dev</code> for Vite during frontend work, or
    <code>npm run build</code> once. Open
    <code>https://koakademy.test/setup</code> to create development data and the first
    administrator.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Validate</h2>
  <pre><code>composer test
vendor/bin/pint --test
npm run build</code></pre>

  <div class="doc-callout doc-callout-note">
    <p class="doc-callout-label">Sharing and PDFs</p>
    <p>
      <code>valet share</code> exposes a public tunnel and requires an external tunnel
      tool or account. PDF generation needs Gotenberg, which Valet does not provide
      — run the Gotenberg Docker image if you work on PDFs, or skip that work locally.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
